Z||000001||Sleeper||10-03-2001||02:42 AM||||cool, but those seats may be a little big for the fiero in the width of the seat. cuz i have the corbeau clubmans and they are a snug but tight little fit and your carreras are almost 2 inches bigger. but its cool man, you'll probably cram them in and get it to work. whos doing the brackets for you?<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho 712 tires, Intrax springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, Addco Front & Rear Swaybars, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines, custom burnt J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||10-03-2001||03:13 AM||||I ordered the seats from a local import store! I assume the brackets are coming straight from the factory. I hope they fit. I emailed the corbeau company and specifically asked them if the carrera seats would fit in my 86 GT and they said yes ,that they would fit but would sit slightly higher than the stock seats. If they don't fit I am going to be really PI$$ED. Well I guess I'll take out the passenger seat tomorrow and try it out!||||reg||1
