Z||000010||reddog||10-08-2001||12:51 AM|||| Lowfunds, the carreras are a little wide in the shoulder area and do overlap a little on the center console. However, the  way the back of the seat is made, sort of rounded like the letter "U" it dosen't hinder the movement of the seat slider and the motion of the seat back position is very close to the same. the outermost part of the shoulder on the seats do make contact on the console and do cause a squeeky noise if you leave them in that position and drive around. Also the seats sit quite a bit higher than stock but I actually like it that way. If you are over 6 feet tall you may not have much head room though. I am trying to get a digital Camera to get some pics if I cant in the next few days then I'll just break out the old 35 mm and take the film to have it converted to disk.     Reddog||||reg||1
